  "confidence": 0.5,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J13", "J17", "U1", "U49"],
      "pins": ["J13.3", "J13.4", "J13.6", "J17.3", "J17.4", "J17.6"],
      "nets": ["NET0069", "NET0020", "NET0196", "NET0122"],
      "observed": "On the CAN BUS sheet the two M12 connectors 'CAN Interface A' (J13) and 'CAN Interface B' (J17) carry an identical set of CAN data nets on pins 3/4/6 (NET0069, NET0020, NET0196); only the per-connector e-stop pin (pin 2: NET0062 vs NET0125) and the power/ESTOP pins differ. The complementary CAN line from the second isolated transceiver (NET0122) does not appear on either connector.",
      "expected": "Per the specification the board provides two *isolated* CAN buses, CAN0 and CAN1, each driven by its own MCP2515 + isolated transceiver and broken out on its own M12 connector ('CAN Interface A' and 'CAN Interface B'). Each connector should therefore carry only that bus's CANH/CANL pair, keeping the two buses separate and galvanically isolated.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "J13 (CAN Interface A) pins: 3=NET0069, 4=NET0020, 6=NET0196; J17 (CAN Interface B) pins: 3=NET0069, 4=NET0020, 6=NET0196 (CAN BUS sheet, connector tiles)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "two isolated CAN buses (CAN0, CAN1), each driven by its own MCP2515 SPI CAN controller ... broken out on M12 circular connectors J2 ('CAN Interface A') and J13 ('CAN Interface B')"}
      ],
      "impact": "CAN0 and CAN1 are merged onto both connectors, destroying the intended galvanic isolation between the two motor/actuator buses and forcing the two Odrive networks to share one bus; one transceiver's CAN line is left unconnected to any connector, so the second bus cannot communicate.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The CAN controllers' 16 MHz crystals and the e-stop/USB/GLOBAL_EN items match the spec or are documented known issues, but the two CAN Interface M12 connectors (J13/J17) appear to be wired with the identical set of CAN data nets, bridging the two supposedly isolated buses and leaving one bus's CAN line unconnected."
}

